Tip

Custom routers are not executed before the system router.

Let’s return to our worked example. Suppose we want to drop traffic from hoenn to both of the other subnets. kanto and johto can obviously be aggregated into 10.0.0.0/23.<br><br>

However, if we add a custom route to hoenn specifying (10.0.0.0/23 → drop), then it will not take effect. Both existing entries in the system router are more specific, matching on /24, and are chosen instead.<br><br>

The correct solution is to create one drop rule per subnet — (subnet:kanto → drop) and (subnet:johto → drop). See Example 1: Creating/assigning routers and routes.
</div>
